@broadcast "Coldwater's Finest - Ride-Along"
@category reality
@length 240
@type scripted

::actors
@actor npc_pd_officer
@alias npc_pd_officer VALE
@actor npc_gate_sergeant
@alias npc_gate_sergeant KESSLER
@actor npc_gate_trooper
@alias npc_gate_trooper QUILL
@actor npc_precinct_guard
@alias npc_precinct_guard KOHL
::endactors

::asset coldwaters_finest_logo

═══════════════════════════════════════════
       ★  C O L D W A T E R ' S  ★
              F I N E S T
      Precinct 9 · Ride-Along Unit
═══════════════════════════════════════════

   "They signed a release. That's the show."

::endasset

::asset finest_booking_card

┌──────────────────────────────────────────┐
│  BOOKING: PRECINCT 9 HOLDING             │
│  STARS: ★★★☆☆         HOLD: 3 MINUTES    │
│  CONTRABAND: SEIZED → EVIDENCE LOCKER    │
│  EFFECTS: RETURNED ON RELEASE*           │
└──────────────────────────────────────────┘
  *Legal items only. Define "legal" at your peril.

::endasset

::scene COLD_OPEN

ROOM zone_mq_precinct_bullpen

EVENT FADE_IN

♪ A cheap, swaggering guitar riff kicks in: four chords, no budget, enormous confidence. ♪

TITLE coldwaters_finest_logo

CAM 1 WIDE basin_night

SHOT
The Basin at night, shot from a low drone: wet asphalt, sodium light, steam coming up through the grates. Somewhere below, a siren starts and then thinks better of it.
SHOT_END

NARRATOR:
Coldwater Basin. Nine-forty PM.

NARRATOR:
Eleven hours into a nine-hour shift, Sergeant Vale is looking for a man who stole a coat.

::scene ROLL_CALL

CAM 2 MEDIUM bullpen

ENTER npc_pd_officer

ACTION npc_pd_officer thumbs through a clipboard that has clearly been rained on.

VALE:
Most nights it's not violence. Most nights it's somebody cold, or somebody owed.

VALE:
People think the stars mean you're dangerous. Stars just mean somebody saw you.

ACTION npc_pd_officer glances at the camera, then away, like he regrets agreeing to this.

VALE:
I've apologised to more people than I've arrested. Put that in the show. They won't.

::scene SEGMENT_ONE

ROOM zone_district_918_919

CAM 3 HANDHELD patrol_stop

LOWER_THIRD
SGT. VALE, PATROL
SHIFT 11:04 · BASIN SOUTH
LOWER_THIRD_END

SHOT
A young runner is up against a wall, hands flat, breathing hard. A vacuum-sealed brick of something green sits on the pavement between him and the officer.
SHOT_END

VALE:
That yours?

VALE:
Don't answer that. It's yours.

ACTION npc_pd_officer crouches, tags the brick, and writes on the tag with a pen that doesn't work until the fourth try.

NARRATOR:
Under Basin ordinance, possession at this weight is three stars and a night in Precinct 9.

NARRATOR:
The suspect's chief concern is not the night in Precinct 9.

VALE:
Hey. Look at me. When did you last back up?

ACTION npc_pd_officer waits. The answer takes a while.

VALE:
Yeah. Well. Try not to die before Thursday, then.

::scene SEGMENT_TWO

CAM 1 WIDE south_gate

SHOT
The South Gate. A queue of people stands in the cold with their arms out while a scanner arch clicks over them, one at a time, forever.
SHOT_END

LOWER_THIRD
SGT. KESSLER & TPR. QUILL
SOUTH GATE CHECKPOINT
LOWER_THIRD_END

ENTER npc_gate_sergeant

KESSLER:
Everybody coming into this city gets searched. Everybody. I've searched the man who signs my cheques.

ENTER npc_gate_trooper

QUILL:
I found a knife once. In a boot. It was a really good find.

ACTION npc_gate_trooper looks at Kessler for confirmation. He does not get it.

KESSLER:
That was nine months ago, Quill.

QUILL:
It was a really good find.

NARRATOR:
Trooper Quill has been at the South Gate for two years and has recovered one knife.

NARRATOR:
He has recovered it repeatedly, in conversation, ever since.

::scene SEGMENT_THREE

ROOM zone_mq_precinct_lobby
ROOM zone_mq_precinct_holding

CAM 2 MEDIUM intake_desk

TITLE finest_booking_card

ENTER npc_precinct_guard

KOHL:
Belt. Laces. Anything sharp, anything that talks to anything else.

ACTION npc_precinct_guard drops a handful of personal effects into a tray with the enthusiasm of a man filing his own paperwork.

KOHL:
Legal property comes back when you walk. Contraband goes in the locker downstairs.

KOHL:
Nothing comes out of the locker downstairs.

SHOT
A folded orange jumpsuit is pushed across the counter. It has been washed so many times it has gone the colour of weak tea.
SHOT_END

NARRATOR:
Three stars. Three minutes a star. In Coldwater, the sentence is served in real time, and the clock does not care that you are bored.

KOHL:
Some of them cry. Some of them sleep. The ones who've been through a vat, they just sit there and stare at the wall like they're waiting for it to buffer.

::scene WRAP

ROOM zone_apt_6

CAM 3 HANDHELD end_of_shift

SHOT
Vale's cruiser, parked. Engine ticking as it cools. He does not get out for a long moment.
SHOT_END

VALE:
People ask if it gets to you.

VALE:
It's a job. You do the job. Then you go home and you sit in your kitchen with the light off for a bit, and then you're fine.

ACTION npc_pd_officer gets out, closes the door quietly, and walks up to apartment six without looking back at the camera.

NARRATOR:
Sergeant Vale will be back on shift in nine hours.

NARRATOR:
Coldwater's Finest. Filmed on location, with the cooperation of people who had no realistic way to decline.

TICKER
